- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/chromaticaberration.html
- Summary (EN): Adds colour fringing that mimics lens behaviour, mainly near the frame edges, by separating and offsetting the red, green and blue channels. A Spectrum mode samples several wavelengths between the channel offsets for smoother fringing.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Chromatic Aberration ajoute des franges de couleur près des bords de l'image en décalant séparément les canaux rouge, vert et bleu, avec un mode spectral plus doux en option.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the original layer", "effect (optional): per-pixel amount controlling the aberration strength", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mode: RGB (offsets channels directly) or Spectrum (simulates wavelengths, converts back to RGB)", "Number of Colors: wavelength samples in Spectrum mode", "Pivot: centre for scale and rotation, default image centre", "Red / Green / Blue (distortion): per-channel scale offsets, defaults -0.15, 0, 0.15", "Global Distortion Scale: zoom-like scale for all channels, default 0.15, shaped by Distortion Scale Mask", "Red / Green / Blue (rotation) and Rotation Scale: rotation in degrees", "Red / Green / Blue (translation), Translation Scale and Translation Scale Mask", "Mask: blends the result with the original, 1 uses only the new result", "Filter: sampling method, default Box"]

- Caveats: ["Spectrum mode and higher Number of Colors cost more to compute", "The page notes that a lens shader at render time is more physically accurate but renders slower"]

